{"availability":"available","full":"PranavThaker/Laptop-Price-Prediction","name":"Laptop-Price-Prediction","description":"Full-stack ML app predicting laptop prices from specs. Random Forest model (R²=0.886) served via FastAPI, React + Vite frontend with dynamic dropdowns sourced from the trained data. Live demo included.","category":"Education","language":"Jupyter Notebook","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-06T10:32:35Z","updated":"2026-09-10T19:28:46Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://laptop-price-prediction-five.vercel.app","topics":["fastapi","full-stack","machine-learning","price-prediction","random-forest","react","scikit-learn","vite"],"demo":"https://laptop-price-prediction-five.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:59.647Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:59.647Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:59.647Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T22:39:59.647Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A full-stack machine learning application that predicts a laptop's price from its hardware and software specifications — a trained Random Forest Regression model served through a FastAPI backend, with a React + Vite frontend for the UI.","The frontend never hardcodes dropdown values. Instead, it pulls valid options live from the backend's /options endpoint, which reflects exactly what the trained model actually saw during training — so users can never submit a combination the model wasn't trained on.","The user fills in specs — company, type, RAM, weight, display, CPU, storage, GPU, OS — on the React frontend. That request hits the FastAPI backend, which:"],"features":["Validates the payload with Pydantic","Re-derives the same engineered features used at training time (pixel density, CPU category, OS category)","Runs the feature vector through the saved Scikit-learn pipeline","Reverses the log-transform applied to the target and returns the predicte